<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">17 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 17 August, from 986 to 1988.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/bulgarians" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bulgarians.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">986 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,040 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Bulgarians defeat Basil II at the Gates of Trajan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the Byzantine–Bulgarian wars, Bulgarian forces defeated the Byzantine army of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basil-ii">Basil II</a> at the Gates of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trajan">Trajan</a>, near present-day Ihtiman, and Basil barely escaped. He later conquered the Bulgarian state, earning the epithet 'the Bulgar-Slayer'.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basil-ii">Basil II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1186">1186 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">840 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Georgenberg Pact promises Styria to the dukes of Austria</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the Georgenberg near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enns-river">Enns</a>, the childless Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottokar-iv-of-styria">Ottokar IV of Styria</a> agreed that his duchy would pass to Duke Leopold V of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-babenberg">Babenbergs</a>, guaranteeing the rights of the Styrian nobles and church. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/styria">Styria</a> joined Austria in 1192.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgenberg-pact">Georgenberg Pact</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottokar-iv-of-styria">Ottokar IV of Styria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1386">1386 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">640 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Karl Thopia allies himself with the Republic of Venice</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Albanian prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karl-thopia">Karl Thopia</a> allied himself with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>, committing to join all the Republic's wars or pay auxiliary funds and supply grain. In return Venice ordered its Adriatic fleet to protect his coasts from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1424">1424 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">602 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">English army defeats a Franco-Scottish force at Verneuil</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Duke of Bedford's army won a bloody victory over French and Scottish troops at Verneuil in Normandy. Hailed as a second <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-agincourt">Agincourt</a>, it secured English control of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> for years.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1488">1488 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">538 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bishop Konrad Bitz dates his preface to the Missale Aboense</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Konrad Bitz, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turku">Turku</a>, dated his introduction to the Missale Aboense, the first book printed for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a>, which was published the same year. Commissioned from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lubeck">Lübeck</a> printer Bartholomeus Ghotan, the missal ran to some 550 folio pages.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1807">1807 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">219 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Robert Fulton's steamboat begins its voyage up the Hudson</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Robert Fulton's North River Steamboat left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> and reached Albany in 32 hours of running. It launched the first commercially successful steamboat service, transforming river travel.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1896">1896 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">130 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bridget Driscoll becomes Britain's first pedestrian killed by a car</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Bridget Driscoll was struck by a demonstration car in the grounds of the Crystal Palace in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>. The coroner hoped such a thing would never happen again.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sukarno proclaims Indonesian independence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Two days after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>'s surrender, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sukarno">Sukarno</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohammad-hatta">Mohammad Hatta</a> proclaimed independence in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jakarta">Jakarta</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> fought to return, but transferred <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> in 1949.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/indonesia">Indonesia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesian-independence">Indonesian independence</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1988">1988 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">38 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pakistan's President Zia ul-Haq dies in a plane crash</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-zia-ul-haq">Muhammad Zia-ul-Haq</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>'s military ruler for eleven years, died when his C-130 crashed near Bahawalpur. The US ambassador also died; the cause has never been established.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a></div></div></li></ol>
